And so, as the stars twinkled brightly in the night sky, they all snuggled up together, dreaming sweet dreams of friendship, bravery, and happiness. The end.', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1476234251651-f353c1b3e3a1?w=800&h=600&fit=crop', 'en', false, 'en', 'classical', 'adapted from Jacob & Wilhelm Grimm', NULL, true, 0);
INSERT INTO stories (id, title, summary, moral, full_content, image_url, language, is_translated, original_language, source_type, author_name, author_id, is_public, like_count) VALUES ('d5ad07ea-ea48-4c9f-bae6-d590cc5bf18a', 'Rapunzel', 'Once upon a time, in a land of lush green forests, there lived a girl named Rapunzel with the most beautiful long hair. Trapped in a tall tower, she longed for friendship and adventure. With the help of a kind prince, she discovers the magic of love and freedom. This is a soothing tale of hope and dreams, perfect for bedtime snuggles.', 'The moral of the story is: "True love and friendship give us the courage to be brave and follow our dreams. Together, we can overcome any challenge and find happiness in the world."', 'Once upon a time, in a peaceful kingdom surrounded by soft rolling hills and fragrant gardens, there lived a girl named Rapunzel. She had the most beautiful hair, flowing like golden sunlight, and it was so long that it could reach all the way to the ground. But Rapunzel lived in a tall, shimmering tower, far away from the world, where she was kept safe by a gentle witch named Gothel.

Gothel loved Rapunzel dearly, for her hair held magical powers that could heal and bring joy. Each day, Gothel would visit her, bringing baskets of fruits and flowers, and they would talk and laugh together. But as the days turned into weeks, and the weeks into months, Rapunzel began to feel a tug in her heart—a longing to see the world outside her tower.

One sunny morning, while singing sweet songs, Rapunzel heard a soft rustle in the bushes below. Curious, she peered out of her high window and spotted a handsome young prince riding his white horse. He was enchanted by her lovely voice and felt a warm glow in his heart. 

“Rapunzel, Rapunzel, let down your hair!” he called out, his voice gentle like a whispering breeze. 

With a flutter of excitement, Rapunzel let her long hair cascade down the tower. The prince climbed up carefully, his heart racing with joy. At last, they were face to face, and Rapunzel’s eyes sparkled like stars. They spent their days laughing and sharing stories, weaving dreams of adventures in the sunlit meadows.

But one day, Gothel discovered their secret. With a frown as dark as storm clouds, she scolded Rapunzel, “You must never see that boy again! You belong to me!” With a wave of her hand, she locked Rapunzel in the tower, and the prince was left heartbroken.

Yet, love is a powerful magic, and the prince could not forget Rapunzel’s laughter. He returned to the tower, calling out her name. Hearing his voice, Rapunzel’s heart soared. With determination, she let down her hair once more, and they climbed together to the safety of a hidden glen.

In this secret place, they found a world filled with blooming flowers and singing birds. They laughed and danced under the warm sun, dreaming of a future where they could be free. But Gothel soon discovered their secret hideaway. In a fit of anger, she cast a spell, causing the prince to fall back, lost in the shadows of the forest.

With tears in her eyes, Rapunzel felt her heart ache. She knew she had to be brave. Using her magic hair, she created a shimmering path of light to guide the prince back. When he returned, their eyes met, and they knew that together they could face anything.

With the warmth of their love and the strength of their hope, they decided to leave the tower behind. Hand in hand, they ventured into the world, where the sun always shone bright and the flowers danced in the gentle breeze. They discovered the beauty of friendship, laughter, and dreams that would last forever.

And so, as the stars twinkled softly in the night sky, Rapunzel and her prince settled down under the vast sky, ready to drift into sweet dreams, knowing they were free, together, forever. With hearts full of love, they whispered, “Goodnight, dear dreams await us.”

And as they closed their eyes, the tower faded away, and they embraced a world filled with endless possibilities. The end.', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1516571748831-5d81767b788d?w=800&h=600&fit=crop', 'en', false, 'en', 'classical', 'adapted from Jacob & Wilhelm Grimm', NULL, true, 0);
INSERT INTO stories (id, title, summary, moral, full_content, image_url, language, is_translated, original_language, source_type, author_name, author_id, is_public, like_count) VALUES ('87366134-e7ce-429a-96c8-f76e9ab7e7b7', 'Rumpelstiltskin', 'In a quiet kingdom, a kind girl named Ella finds herself in a tricky situation when she must spin straw into gold with the help of a mysterious little creature. With a warm heart and clever mind, she embarks on a journey to uncover his name, learning about friendship and bravery along the way. This enchanting tale teaches us the power of kindness and the magic of believing in ourselves.', 'The moral of the story is: "True friendship and kindness can help us overcome big challenges, and it''s important to believe in ourselves and never give up."', 'Once upon a time, in a peaceful kingdom surrounded by rolling hills and soft, whispering winds, there lived a kind girl named Ella. She was known for her gentle spirit and bright smile. One day, while wandering through the meadows, Ella accidentally caught the attention of a greedy king who loved shiny things. He ordered her to spin straw into gold, thinking he could make a fortune from her talents.

Ella felt scared and alone in a great big room filled with heaps of straw. "How can I ever do this?" she whispered to herself, her heart pounding with worry. Just as she was about to lose hope, a cheerful little creature appeared. With a twinkle in his eye and a mischievous grin, he said, "Don''t worry, dear Ella! I can help you!"

"Who are you?" Ella asked, surprised but curious. 

"I’m Rumpelstiltskin, and I can spin this straw into gold for you!" he exclaimed, dancing in delight. Ella watched in wonder as the little creature twirled and spun, turning the straw into shimmering gold threads that sparkled like the stars in the night sky.

The king was thrilled with the gold and demanded more. So, every night, Ella and Rumpelstiltskin worked together, and he spun more straw into gold, while Ella grew more comfortable with her new friend. They laughed and shared stories, and Ella learned that kindness and warmth made their work easier.

However, the king soon grew greedy and wanted even more gold. "You must spin all the straw in the kingdom!" he ordered, and poor Ella''s heart sank. Rumpelstiltskin came to her rescue once more, but this time he asked for something in return. "I will help you, but you must promise to give me your first-born child!" he declared, winking playfully.

Ella was taken aback. She thought of her dreams of one day having a family, and hesitated for a moment. But as they spun and laughed, she agreed, thinking it was a long way off. Day after day, they worked together until the king had all the gold he could wish for, and he married Ella, believing her to be the most talented girl in the land.

As time passed, Ella and the king welcomed a beautiful baby into their home. Ella was filled with joy, but she also remembered her promise to Rumpelstiltskin. One day, the little creature returned, and Ella''s heart ached with sadness. "Please, I cannot bear to part with my child," she pleaded.

Rumpelstiltskin, seeing the tears in her eyes, softened. "I see you care for your little one deeply. How about we make a deal?" he said gently. "If you can guess my name within three days, you may keep your child."

Ella nodded, determined to solve the riddle. That night, she searched high and low for clues, asking the birds and the flowers, but no one knew the name of the mysterious creature. On the final day, as she walked through the forest, she heard a delightful sound—a joyful song. Following the melody, she stumbled upon Rumpelstiltskin, dancing and singing in a glade.

With her heart full of hope, Ella listened closely and suddenly realized, "Your name is Rumpelstiltskin!" she called out with glee. The little creature stopped, his eyes wide with surprise. 

"You guessed it!" he laughed softly, his heart light. "You have proven your cleverness and courage. As a gift, you may keep your child, and I shall take my leave with joy in my heart."

And so, Rumpelstiltskin danced away into the magical forest, leaving Ella and her family filled with love and happiness. From that day on, they cherished one another, and every night, as they drifted off to sleep, they whispered tales of their adventures and dreams, knowing that kindness and cleverness could conquer all. 

And in that gentle kingdom, under a blanket of stars, they lived happily ever after, surrounded by the softest dreams and the sweetest love.', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1518709594023-6eab9bab7b23?w=800&h=600&fit=crop', 'en', false, 'en', 'classical', 'adapted from Jacob & Wilhelm Grimm', NULL, true, 0);
INSERT INTO stories (id, title, summary, moral, full_content, image_url, language, is_translated, original_language, source_type, author_name, author_id, is_public, like_count) VALUES ('03bc9663-9c14-42a1-8574-a87261c4ce00', 'The Frog Prince', 'In a serene kingdom, a kind princess befriends a lonely frog after he retrieves her precious golden ball. Through a promise of friendship, the frog transforms into a handsome prince, teaching the importance of keeping promises and looking beyond appearances. Their bond blossoms, leading to a peaceful and joyful ending as they discover the beauty of true friendship.', 'Always keep your promises, for true friendship is a treasure that brings joy and magic to our lives. Remember, the kindness we show can reveal the best in others!', 'Once upon a time, in a peaceful kingdom, there lived a lovely princess with a heart full of kindness. One sunny day, as she played by a shimmering pond, her favorite golden ball fell into the water with a soft plop. She was heartbroken and began to cry, for the ball was not just any toy; it was a treasure she cherished dearly.

Just then, a gentle frog emerged from the water. With big, round eyes and a soothing voice, he said, "Don’t be sad, dear princess. I can help you retrieve your ball from the pond. But in return, you must promise to be my friend."

The princess, quite surprised by the frog''s words, nodded eagerly, thinking that this was a small price to pay for her beloved ball. "Of course, I promise!" she exclaimed, her heart lightening at the thought of having her treasured toy back.

With a swift leap, the frog plunged into the water and soon resurfaced, holding the golden ball gently in his mouth. The princess clapped her hands with joy, thanking the frog for his kindness. But when she looked at him, she felt a little awkward. The frog was not what she imagined as a friend.

In her excitement, the princess turned to leave, forgetting her promise. "Wait!" the frog called out after her. "You promised to be my friend!" But the princess hurried home, leaving the frog behind.

Days passed, and the princess couldn’t shake off the feeling of guilt. The frog had been so kind, and she had not kept her promise. One evening, as she sat by her window, she heard a soft knock. Curious, she opened the door and found the frog sitting on her doorstep, his eyes sparkling with hope.

Remembering her promise, she invited him in. The frog hopped inside, and as they sat together, he began to share stories about the wonders of the pond and the creatures who lived there. The princess listened, enchanted by his tales. She realized that he was not just a frog, but a true friend.

Her heart warmed, and she felt a sense of peace wash over her. Just then, the frog said, "If you truly wish to be my friend, you must promise to never forget your word." The princess nodded, her heart filled with sincerity, and in that moment, she felt something magical happen.

With a bright light and a gentle shimmer, the frog transformed into a handsome prince! The princess gasped in delight, for now she understood that true beauty lies within. The prince smiled, his kind eyes sparkling. "Thank you for keeping your promise, dear princess. You have set me free with your kindness."

From that day on, the princess and the prince became the best of friends. They spent their days exploring the kingdom, sharing laughter, and spreading joy wherever they went. They learned together that keeping promises and cherishing friendships were the most valuable treasures of all.

As the sun set, painting the sky in soft hues of orange and pink, the princess and the prince returned to the pond where their friendship began. They sat side by side, watching the stars twinkle in the night sky, feeling grateful for the magical bond they had formed.

And so, in the warmth of their friendship, they drifted off to sleep, dreaming of new adventures together, knowing that each day would be filled with love and laughter. The end.', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1516979187457-637abb4f9353?w=800&h=600&fit=crop', 'en', false, 'en', 'classical', 'adapted from Jacob & Wilhelm Grimm', NULL, true, 0);
INSERT INTO stories (id, title, summary, moral, full_content, image_url, language, is_translated, original_language, source_type, author_name, author_id, is_public, like_count) VALUES ('b7bff2be-9688-495a-98db-b512cda4a16e', 'The Golden Goose', 'Once upon a time, there was a kind boy named Gilly who lived in a small village. One day, he discovered a magical golden goose that brought happiness wherever it went. As Gilly shared his newfound friend with others, he learned the importance of kindness and friendship. Join Gilly on his gentle adventure, filled with laughter and joy, as he finds his way to a peaceful ending under the stars.', 'Always share kindness and friendship, for they can bring joy to everyone around you. Remember, a little magic can be found in the happiness you create for others!', 'Once upon a time, in a cozy little village, there lived a kind-hearted boy named Gilly. Gilly was known for his gentle spirit and warm smile, always ready to lend a helping hand to anyone in need. One sunny day, while wandering through the woods, Gilly stumbled upon a shimmering golden feather. Curious and enchanted, he followed the trail of feathers deeper into the forest.

As he walked, he spotted a beautiful golden goose happily waddling by a sparkling pond. The goose had feathers that glimmered like the sun, and Gilly felt an instant connection. He approached the goose and, to his surprise, the friendly bird began to honk joyfully. Gilly knew this was no ordinary goose; it was magical!

Excitedly, Gilly decided to take the golden goose back to his village to share his new friend with everyone. As they walked together, the townspeople gathered around, intrigued by the lovely goose. But when they tried to touch it, something wonderful happened. Each person who reached for the goose found themselves gently stuck to it! 

“Oh dear!” exclaimed the baker, who had a flour-covered apron. “I only wanted to pet it!”

One by one, the villagers joined the cheerful parade, all holding on to each other and the golden goose. Gilly giggled as the entire village followed him, creating a line of laughter and joy. They danced and sang, celebrating the magic of friendship that the golden goose brought to their lives.

As they strolled through the village, Gilly noticed how the golden goose made everyone feel warm and happy inside. The children laughed and clapped, while the elders smiled with delight. Gilly felt a sense of joy knowing that sharing the magical goose had made everyone’s day brighter.

Eventually, the group wandered to a peaceful meadow filled with colorful flowers and twinkling fireflies. The sun began to set, painting the sky with shades of pink and orange. Gilly knew it was time to say goodbye to the golden goose, but he felt no sadness, only gratitude.

The golden goose honked softly, as if understanding Gilly''s heart. With a final twinkle of its feathers, it spread its wings and flew high into the sky, leaving a trail of golden sparkles behind. Gilly waved goodbye, knowing that the magic of kindness would always remain in his heart and in the hearts of his friends.

As the stars began to twinkle in the night sky, Gilly returned home, feeling peaceful and content. He snuggled into his cozy bed, surrounded by the happiness he had shared with others. With a heart full of love, he closed his eyes, drifting off to sleep, dreaming of golden goose adventures and the joy of friendship.

And so, dear little ones, remember that kindness is a magical thing that can bring happiness to everyone. Sleep tight, and may your dreams be filled with laughter and love, just like Gilly’s. Goodnight.', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1604004555489-723a93d6ce74?w=800&h=600&fit=crop', 'en', false, 'en', 'classical', 'adapted from Jacob & Wilhelm Grimm', NULL, true, 0);
INSERT INTO stories (id, title, summary, moral, full_content, image_url, language, is_translated, original_language, source_type, author_name, author_id, is_public, like_count) VALUES ('b718a505-1fb4-474d-bb11-6fa9660bff6b', 'The Fisherman and His Wife', 'In a quaint little village by the sea, a kind fisherman and his wife discover a magical fish that grants wishes. As the wife dreams of a better life, her wishes grow bigger and bigger, leading to unexpected lessons about contentment and gratitude. Join them on this enchanting journey, where wishes come true, but joy is found in the simplest of things.', 'True happiness comes from loving what you have and being content with each other, not from wishing for more. Always cherish the simple joys in life!', 'Once upon a time, in a peaceful little village by the shimmering sea, there lived a kind fisherman and his gentle wife. They had a modest home, but they were happy and loved each other dearly. One sunny day, while casting his net into the sparkling waves, the fisherman caught a beautiful fish unlike any he had ever seen. The fish shimmered like the stars and spoke to him in a soft, soothing voice.

"Please, kind fisherman," the fish said, "if you let me go, I will grant you a wish!" The fisherman, surprised but wise, thought about his humble life. He looked back at his loving wife and said, "Thank you, dear fish, but I cannot wish for anything. I am content."

The fish smiled and swam away, happy to be free.

When the fisherman returned home, he told his wife about the magical fish. She was intrigued and said, "Oh, dear husband, let us ask for a cozy cottage instead of our little home. It would be so lovely!" The fisherman, wanting to make her happy, agreed and returned to the sea.

He called out to the fish, and soon it appeared. "Dear fish, my wife wishes for a cozy cottage," he said.

In a flash, the fish granted the wish, and they found themselves in a lovely cottage with a beautiful garden. The wife was delighted, but soon she began to desire even more. "My dear fisherman," she said, "I want to be a queen! Please, ask the fish for this wish!"

Reluctantly, the fisherman went back to the sea again. He called for the fish and said, "Oh fish, my wife wishes to be a queen."

The fish granted the wish, and soon the wife was dressed in royal robes, sitting on a grand throne. But even as a queen, she was not satisfied. "I want to be the most powerful queen in the land!" she exclaimed. "Go back to the fish and ask for this!"

With a heavy heart, the fisherman returned to the sea. He asked the fish, and once again, the wish was granted. But now, the wife was not just a queen; she was the ruler of all. Yet, her heart was still restless.

"I want to rule the stars and the moon!" she declared. The fisherman was worried but did as she wished. He went back to the fish, who was now looking quite weary from granting all these wishes. "Oh fish, my wife wishes to rule the stars and the moon," he said softly.

The fish paused for a moment, then replied gently, "Your wishes have grown bigger, dear fisherman. It is important to remember what truly makes you happy."

With a wave of its fin, the fish granted the wish, and suddenly, the wife found herself alone, back in their little hut, just as they had started.

The fisherman, finding his wife distressed, took her hands and said, "We have each other, and that is the greatest treasure of all. Let us be happy with what we have."

With a soft smile, she realized that her heart was full when she was with her beloved fisherman. They embraced, feeling grateful for their simple life, and as the stars twinkled above, they fell into a peaceful sleep, knowing that true happiness comes from love and contentment.

And so, the fisherman and his wife lived happily ever after, cherishing each moment together. The end.', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1476234251651-f353c1b3e3a1?w=800&h=600&fit=crop', 'en', false, 'en', 'classical', 'adapted from Jacob & Wilhelm Grimm', NULL, true, 0);
INSERT INTO stories (id, title, summary, moral, full_content, image_url, language, is_translated, original_language, source_type, author_name, author_id, is_public, like_count) VALUES ('aa47b4dc-9327-4139-8eb8-fdc1ef6535f6', 'The Twelve Dancing Princesses', 'In a charming kingdom, twelve lovely princesses mysteriously wear out their shoes every night. A brave young man sets out to discover their secret, guided by kindness and cleverness. Through enchanting adventures, he uncovers the truth and brings peace to the kingdom, allowing everyone to rest easy once more. Join us on this magical journey filled with mystery and joy.', 'The magic of kindness and friendship can help us solve even the biggest mysteries. Always be brave and share joy with others, for together we can find happiness!', 'Once upon a time, in a peaceful kingdom nestled between soft, rolling hills, there lived twelve princesses. Each princess was as lovely as a flower, with laughter that sparkled like stars in the night sky. However, there was a puzzling mystery in the castle: every morning, the princesses would wake up to find their beautiful shoes worn out and tattered.

The king, a gentle and wise ruler, was deeply concerned. He summoned the bravest knights in the land, offering a grand reward to anyone who could uncover the secret of the worn-out shoes. But try as they might, no one could solve the mystery, and the knights soon returned home, tired and confused.

One day, a kind-hearted young man named Henry, who lived in a small village nearby, heard the tale of the twelve princesses. Intrigued and filled with curiosity, he decided to embark on a journey to the castle. With courage in his heart, he arrived at the grand castle gates and asked the king if he could help.

The king, grateful for Henry''s determination, welcomed him warmly. "You may stay in the castle tonight, my dear boy," said the king. "But be sure to keep a watchful eye on my daughters. They must not be allowed to leave the castle after nightfall."

That evening, as the sun dipped below the horizon and the stars began to twinkle, Henry settled himself in a cozy chair near the princesses'' chamber. He listened to their giggles and whispers, wondering what adventures awaited them.

As the clock struck midnight, Henry noticed the princesses quietly rising from their beds, their eyes sparkling with excitement. They tiptoed past him, unaware of his presence, and ventured out of the castle. Henry quickly followed them, his heart racing with curiosity.

To his astonishment, the princesses led him to a hidden glade filled with shimmering lights. There, he saw magical creatures dancing gracefully under the moonlight. The princesses twirled and spun, their laughter echoing through the trees. Henry realized they had been visiting a secret enchanted realm, where they could dance as freely as the stars above.

As the night wore on, Henry approached the princesses and gently asked, "Why do you dance every night?" The eldest princess smiled and replied, "We are under an enchantment that makes us dance until dawn. Only a kind heart can help us find our way back home."

Henry thought for a moment and then proposed a plan. "What if we invite the magical creatures to dance with us in the castle? It could be a joyful celebration, and perhaps the enchantment will break!" The princesses loved the idea, and together, they returned to the castle.

With the help of the magical creatures, a grand ball was held in the castle. The music filled the air, and everyone danced with joy. As the night passed, the enchantment slowly faded away, and the princesses found themselves no longer compelled to dance. They thanked Henry for his cleverness and kindness.

The king was overjoyed and rewarded Henry with gratitude and friendship. The castle was filled with laughter and happiness, and the princesses could now enjoy peaceful nights of restful sleep.

From that day on, the twelve princesses no longer wore out their shoes, and they shared their enchanting stories with everyone, reminding them of the magic of kindness. And so, in the soft glow of moonlight, they all lived happily ever after, with dreams as sweet as the dances they had shared.

As the stars winked down upon them, the kingdom settled into a peaceful slumber, knowing that the magic of friendship and love would always light their way. And with that, dear little ones, it''s time to close your eyes and dream sweet dreams.', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1516571748831-5d81767b788d?w=800&h=600&fit=crop', 'en', false, 'en', 'classical', 'adapted from Jacob & Wilhelm Grimm', NULL, true, 0);
INSERT INTO stories (id, title, summary, moral, full_content, image_url, language, is_translated, original_language, source_type, author_name, author_id, is_public, like_count) VALUES ('43c9720b-47f8-40a6-b8bf-3ad261b703be', 'The Goose Girl', 'In a tranquil kingdom, a kind princess is betrayed and forced to become a goose girl. With the help of her loyal friends, she finds a way to reclaim her true identity. This heartwarming tale teaches us about courage, friendship, and the power of being true to oneself, all wrapped in a soothing bedtime story.', 'Always be true to yourself and show kindness to others, for love and courage can help you overcome any challenge. Remember, true friends will always believe in you!', 'Once upon a time, in a peaceful kingdom, there lived a gentle princess named Emma. She loved to roam the meadows, listen to the soft whispers of the wind, and tend to her beautiful garden. One day, her mother, the queen, sent her on a journey to meet a prince from a faraway land.

On her way, Emma met a cunning woman who pretended to be a wise old lady. This woman had dark intentions and tricked Emma into switching places with her daughter, a girl who looked just like the princess. The next thing Emma knew, she was dressed in simple clothes, tending to a flock of geese, while the cunning woman took her place in the palace.

Though Emma was sad and lonely, she had a heart full of hope. She cared for the geese with love, and they soon became her dear friends. Every evening, as the sun dipped below the horizon, the geese would gather around her, honking softly, as if to comfort her. 

One day, while tending to the geese, Emma met a kind-hearted prince who often rode through the meadow. He noticed how gracefully she moved among her feathered friends, and he was captivated. The prince would come to visit her, and they shared stories of their dreams and wishes. Emma told him of her true identity, and the prince believed her, for he saw the kindness and strength in her heart.

To help Emma reclaim her rightful place, the prince devised a clever plan. Together, they would reveal the truth. He arranged a grand ball at the palace and invited everyone, including the cunning woman. Emma, with the help of her loyal geese, crafted a beautiful gown adorned with soft feathers and shining pearls. The gown shimmered like the stars, and Emma looked radiant.

On the night of the ball, Emma arrived at the palace, her heart racing with excitement and a sprinkle of nervousness. The guests gasped in awe at her beauty, and the prince smiled warmly at her. As the evening unfolded, the cunning woman, unaware of Emma''s true identity, tried to deceive everyone still. But when the prince spoke up, sharing the truth about Emma’s bravery and kindness, the guests began to murmur.

With the help of her friends, the geese, and the courage she had gathered, Emma stood tall. She told her story, and everyone listened with wide eyes. They learned how she had been tricked and how she had never lost hope. The kindness of her heart shone through, and soon, the truth was clear to all.

As the moon lit up the night sky, Emma was welcomed back to her rightful place as the beloved princess. The kingdom rejoiced, and the cunning woman, realizing her plans had failed, was banished from the land. Emma’s heart swelled with joy, and she promised to always be kind and true to herself.

From that day forward, Emma ruled the kingdom with grace, surrounded by her loyal friends and the gentle geese. Each night, as she looked up at the stars, she remembered the lessons she had learned: that love, courage, and being true to oneself are the greatest treasures of all.

And so, in her cozy castle, Emma drifted off to sleep, her heart full of dreams and her spirit at peace, ready for the adventures that tomorrow would bring. The end.', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1518709594023-6eab9bab7b23?w=800&h=600&fit=crop', 'en', false, 'en', 'classical', 'adapted from Jacob & Wilhelm Grimm', NULL, true, 0);
INSERT INTO stories (id, title, summary, moral, full_content, image_url, language, is_translated, original_language, source_type, author_name, author_id, is_public, like_count) VALUES ('e3dc31e7-c861-4613-93a8-be590dc4be07', 'The Elves and the Shoemaker', 'Once upon a time, in a cozy little village, there lived a kind shoemaker who struggled to make ends meet. One night, enchanting little elves appeared to help him craft beautiful shoes while he slept. With their magic touch, the shoemaker''s fortune began to change, leading to a heartwarming tale of kindness and gratitude that reminds us all of the magic of giving and friendship.', 'Helping others can create magic in our lives, and kindness always brings joy to those around us. Remember, a grateful heart and sharing what we have can make the world a happier place!', 'In a quaint little village, there lived a gentle shoemaker named Mr. Finn. He had a warm heart and loved to create beautiful shoes, but times were tough, and he could hardly make enough to feed himself.

Every evening, after finishing his work, Mr. Finn would look at his worn-out shoes and sigh. "If only I could make just one pair of lovely shoes to sell!" he would whisper to himself, feeling a little sad but always hopeful.

One night, as the moonlight softly filled his tiny workshop, Mr. Finn laid down to rest, dreaming of bright futures and happy customers. Little did he know, while he slept, magic was stirring in his little shop.

As the clock struck midnight, tiny figures appeared in the glow of the moonlight. They were delightful little elves, no taller than a shoelace! With nimble fingers and joyful hearts, they hopped to work. They gathered the finest leather and began to cut, stitch, and shape the beautiful shoes that Mr. Finn had only dreamed of creating.

In the morning, when Mr. Finn awoke, he was amazed to find a stunning pair of shoes neatly placed on his workbench. They sparkled in the sunlight, and he could hardly believe his eyes! He quickly set the shoes in his shop, and before long, a customer arrived. "Oh! What exquisite shoes!" the lady exclaimed, and she bought them right away.

With the money he earned, Mr. Finn felt a glimmer of hope. That night, he laid down again with a smile on his face, whispering a heartfelt ‘thank you’ to the magical beings he didn’t know were helping him.

Night after night, the elves returned, crafting shoes that were even more enchanting than the last. With each pair, Mr. Finn’s shop flourished, and he became known far and wide for his beautiful creations. He was filled with joy and gratitude, but he was also curious about his tiny helpers.

One evening, he decided to stay awake and see who was making the magic happen. He hid behind a curtain, his heart beating with excitement. As midnight approached, the little elves appeared, singing a merry tune and dancing as they worked.

Mr. Finn couldn’t contain his happiness. He clapped his hands, startling the elves! They turned to him, their tiny faces glowing with surprise.

“Thank you, dear friends, for all your help! I have been so grateful for your kindness,” he said warmly. The elves smiled, their eyes twinkling like stars. “We love to help those in need,” they replied, their voices soft like a gentle breeze. “But now we must go. We have other places to help.”

Mr. Finn thought for a moment and then said, “Please, take this gift as a token of my gratitude.” He handed them a pair of the most beautiful shoes he had ever made, crafted with love and care.

The elves were overjoyed! They danced around the workshop, their laughter filling the air like soft music. “Thank you, dear shoemaker! You have made us very happy!” And with that, they waved goodbye and vanished into the night.

From that day on, the shoemaker’s shop continued to thrive. He never forgot the kindness of the little elves and often shared his good fortune with those in need in the village. As he fell asleep each night, he would smile, knowing that magic exists in friendship and generosity.

And so, with a heart full of joy, Mr. Finn slept soundly, dreaming of all the adventures still to come. And perhaps, just perhaps, he would hear the soft tapping of tiny feet and the whispers of magic in the night.

The end.', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1516979187457-637abb4f9353?w=800&h=600&fit=crop', 'en', false, 'en', 'classical', 'adapted from Jacob & Wilhelm Grimm', NULL, true, 0);
INSERT INTO stories (id, title, summary, moral, full_content, image_url, language, is_translated, original_language, source_type, author_name, author_id, is_public, like_count) VALUES ('18f11d79-fe78-4591-862d-0e751f4f7e75', 'Aladdin and the Magic Lamp', 'In a bustling market, a kind-hearted boy named Aladdin discovers a magical lamp that holds a gentle genie. With the help of the genie, Aladdin learns the importance of kindness and bravery, leading to wonderful adventures. As the stars twinkle above, Aladdin finds happiness and peace, reminding us that true magic comes from within.', 'The true magic in life comes from being kind and sharing love with others. When we care for those around us, we create happiness that can light up the world!', 'Once upon a time, in a lively city filled with colorful markets and fragrant spices, there lived a kind-hearted boy named Aladdin. He had a curious spirit and a smile that could light up even the gloomiest of days. Aladdin often wandered through the bustling streets, dreaming of adventures beyond the horizon.

One sunny afternoon, while exploring a hidden corner of the market, Aladdin stumbled upon an old, dusty lamp. With a gentle rub, to his surprise, a swirl of mist filled the air, and a gentle genie appeared, glowing with warmth and kindness.

"Hello, dear Aladdin!" said the genie, his voice like soft music. "I am here to grant you three wishes, but remember, the greatest magic comes from the heart."

Aladdin''s eyes sparkled with excitement. He thought carefully about his first wish. "I wish for a beautiful home where I can always feel safe and happy!" he declared. The genie waved his hand, and in an instant, a cozy little house appeared, surrounded by blooming flowers and tall trees.

As Aladdin settled into his new home, he realized his next wish should be something truly special. "I wish for my family to be together and always share joy!" he said, his heart full of love. The genie nodded, and soon, Aladdin''s family arrived, laughing and hugging, filling the house with warmth and happiness.

Now, Aladdin had one wish left. He pondered what to ask for, thinking of all the wonderful things he had already received. Then he remembered the people in his city who needed help. "Oh, gentle genie, I wish to bring happiness to everyone in my town!" he exclaimed.

With a twinkle in his eyes, the genie waved his hands once more. Suddenly, the streets were filled with laughter, and colorful balloons floated high above. The townspeople danced and celebrated, their hearts filled with joy and gratitude. Aladdin felt a warm glow inside, knowing he had shared the magic of kindness.

As the sun began to set, painting the sky with shades of pink and gold, Aladdin thanked the genie for his wishes. "You have shown me that true magic lies in caring for others and sharing love."

The genie smiled and replied, "Remember, dear Aladdin, the magic you hold within you is the most powerful of all."

With that, the genie gently faded away, leaving behind a sense of peace and happiness. Aladdin snuggled into his cozy home, surrounded by his loving family and the laughter of friends. The stars twinkled brightly in the night sky, and Aladdin closed his eyes, dreaming of all the adventures yet to come.

And so, dear child, as you drift off to sleep, remember that kindness and love are the greatest treasures of all. Sweet dreams await you, just like Aladdin''s magical journey, where every wish can come true with a heart full of love.', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1604004555489-723a93d6ce74?w=800&h=600&fit=crop', 'en', false, 'en', 'classical', 'adapted from One Thousand and One Nights', NULL, true, 0);
INSERT INTO stories (id, title, summary, moral, full_content, image_url, language, is_translated, original_language, source_type, author_name, author_id, is_public, like_count) VALUES ('c0d2e77a-2691-4ecc-ba3d-dd10203cfc81', 'Ali Baba and the Forty Thieves', 'In a quiet village, a kind woodcutter named Ali Baba discovers a secret cave filled with treasures. With the help of his clever sister, they outsmart the greedy thieves and learn that friendship and family are the greatest treasures of all. Join Ali Baba on this gentle adventure that teaches us the value of kindness and cleverness, perfect for sweet dreams.', 'The true treasure in life comes from being kind and sharing with others. Remember, friendships and love are more valuable than gold and gems!', 'Once upon a time, in a peaceful village, there lived a humble woodcutter named Ali Baba. He was known for his gentle heart and kind spirit. Every day, he would wander into the forest, where he would gather wood to sell in the market. One day, while he was working, he noticed something unusual: a group of forty thieves riding on their horses, their saddlebags filled with sparkling treasures.

Curious, Ali Baba quietly followed them. He watched as they approached a large, moss-covered rock. To his amazement, the leader of the thieves called out, "Open Sesame!" And just like magic, the rock slid aside to reveal a hidden cave brimming with gold, silver, and precious gems. Ali Baba''s eyes widened with wonder, but he knew he had to be careful.

Once the thieves left, Ali Baba approached the cave. He took a deep breath and whispered, "Open Sesame!" The rock moved, allowing him to enter the cave. Inside, he could hardly believe his eyes! Piles of glittering treasure sparkled in the warm light. He quickly filled his own bag with enough gold and silver to share with his family.

When he returned home, Ali Baba shared his secret with his clever sister, Morgiana, who always had a bright idea. Together, they decided that they would keep the treasure safe and use it to help others in their village. Morgiana was wise and knew that the thieves would soon return, so they had to be careful.

The next day, the thieves realized that their treasure was missing. They were furious! They decided to find the thief who had dared to take their gold. The clever Morgiana thought of a plan to protect her brother. She disguised herself and listened carefully to the thieves as they plotted to catch Ali Baba.

Morgiana used her cunning to outsmart the thieves at every turn. She tricked them into thinking she was one of them, and one by one, she helped them get lost in the forest. Each time they thought they were close to finding Ali Baba, Morgiana would lead them astray, making them chase their tails in circles!

Finally, the leader of the thieves was so frustrated that he decided to confront Ali Baba directly. But Morgiana was ready. She had prepared a delicious feast and invited the leader into their home, where they shared stories and laughter. The leader was so enchanted by Morgiana''s kindness that he forgot all about the treasure!

In the end, Ali Baba and Morgiana taught the thieves about kindness, sharing, and the joy of friendship. The thieves decided to leave their life of greed behind and became friends with Ali Baba and Morgiana, helping the village thrive with their newfound treasures.

As the sun set over the village, Ali Baba, Morgiana, and their new friends gathered around a warm fire, sharing stories and laughter under the twinkling stars. They learned that true treasure lies not in gold and gems, but in the love and joy we share with others.

As the night grew quiet and the moon shone softly in the sky, Ali Baba and Morgiana drifted off to sleep, dreaming of their adventures and the many wonderful friendships they had made. And so, in their hearts, they knew that kindness was the greatest treasure of all. 

Goodnight, little dreamers, may you also find joy in kindness and the treasures of friendship.', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1476234251651-f353c1b3e3a1?w=800&h=600&fit=crop', 'en', false, 'en', 'classical', 'adapted from One Thousand and One Nights', NULL, true, 0);
INSERT INTO stories (id, title, summary, moral, full_content, image_url, language, is_translated, original_language, source_type, author_name, author_id, is_public, like_count) VALUES ('f930bcb7-ebf2-46f9-b428-1bd7578f87b4', 'The Seven Voyages of Sinbad', 'Join Sinbad, a brave sailor, as he embarks on seven magical voyages across shimmering seas filled with wonders and friendly creatures. Each adventure teaches him about courage, friendship, and the beauty of the world. As he returns home, he finds peace and joy, ready to share his tales under the starry sky. Perfect for bedtime, this gentle story whispers of dreams and adventures.', 'Always be kind and open your heart to new friends, for every adventure teaches us something special. Remember, love and friendship will always guide you home.', 'Once upon a time, in a bustling town by the sea, there lived a kind-hearted sailor named Sinbad. He loved the ocean and dreamed of wonderful adventures. One bright morning, he decided to set sail on a grand journey across the magical seas.

On his first voyage, as the gentle waves rocked his ship, Sinbad found himself on an enchanting island. There, he discovered giant creatures that looked like friendly elephants! With their soft eyes and playful trumpets, they welcomed him and showed him the secrets of their land. Together, they danced under the sun and shared stories. Soon, it was time for Sinbad to leave, but he promised to return one day.

On his second voyage, Sinbad sailed to an island filled with beautiful flowers and sweet fruits. The kind-hearted people there invited him to a feast, where they shared laughter and delicious treats. Sinbad felt warmth in his heart as he made new friends. They taught him about kindness and sharing, and he left with a basket of fruits and a promise to never forget them.

The third adventure took Sinbad to a mysterious place where the stars seemed to twinkle brighter than ever before. He met a wise old man who told him tales of the stars and their magic. Sinbad listened closely, learning about the wonders of the universe. As he sailed away, he felt grateful for the wisdom he gained.

On his fourth voyage, a gentle storm brewed, and Sinbad found himself surrounded by waves that sparkled like diamonds. But he was not afraid. He remembered the lessons from his friends and the wise man. With courage in his heart, he steered his ship safely through the storm, and the skies cleared to reveal a beautiful rainbow. Sinbad smiled, knowing that with bravery, he could face any challenge.

His fifth adventure brought him to the Land of Dreams, where he met friendly creatures who painted the skies with colors. They invited him to a magical party under the stars, where everyone danced and sang. Sinbad felt joy filling his heart, and he realized that dreams are meant to be shared with others.

On the sixth voyage, Sinbad discovered a hidden underwater kingdom. There, he swam with playful dolphins and learned to communicate with the fish. The sea creatures shared their home with him, showing him the importance of caring for the ocean. Sinbad promised to always respect the sea and its wonders.

Finally, on his seventh voyage, Sinbad returned home. As he stepped onto the familiar shores, he looked up at the twinkling stars and felt a sense of peace. He had seen so much, made wonderful friends, and learned valuable lessons along the way. Sitting on the beach, he shared his adventures with the children of his town, who listened with wide eyes and smiles.

As the moon shone brightly above, Sinbad realized that every adventure he took brought him closer to home and to the people he loved. With a heart full of joy and stories to tell, he closed his eyes, feeling the soft breeze and listening to the gentle waves lapping at the shore. And as he drifted off to sleep, he dreamed of new adventures that awaited him, knowing that no matter where he went, the love of home would always guide him back.

And so, dear children, as you snuggle into your beds tonight, remember that every dream can take you on a wonderful journey. Close your eyes, and let your dreams sail you away, just like Sinbad, to magical lands of adventure and friendship. Goodnight.', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1516571748831-5d81767b788d?w=800&h=600&fit=crop', 'en', false, 'en', 'classical', 'adapted from One Thousand and One Nights', NULL, true, 0);
INSERT INTO stories (id, title, summary, moral, full_content, image_url, language, is_translated, original_language, source_type, author_name, author_id, is_public, like_count) VALUES ('3c6fcd3e-a990-4848-81c1-9090bb562896', 'The Fisherman and the Genie', 'In a calm and shimmering sea, a kind-hearted fisherman discovers a mysterious bottle. When he opens it, a gentle genie appears, ready to grant him wishes. Together, they learn about kindness and gratitude, and the fisherman discovers that true happiness comes from sharing. Join them on this magical adventure as they find peace and friendship in the twilight of the day.', 'The true magic of happiness comes from sharing and caring for others. When we help our friends and community, we create a world full of joy and love!', 'Once upon a time, in a small village by the sparkling sea, there lived a kind-hearted fisherman named Ali. Every morning, he would cast his net into the calm waters, hoping to catch enough fish to feed his family. One sunny day, as he pulled in his net, he felt something heavy caught within it.

Curious, Ali tugged and tugged until he finally pulled up a shiny bottle. It was beautiful, with delicate engravings that shimmered in the sunlight. "What a lovely treasure!" he exclaimed, his eyes sparkling with wonder. But as he cleaned the bottle with his cloth, a sudden puff of mist burst forth, swirling around him like a gentle breeze.

To Ali''s surprise, from the mist emerged a magnificent genie. The genie had twinkling eyes and a warm smile that lit up the entire beach. "Thank you for freeing me, dear fisherman!" the genie said in a voice as soft as a lullaby. "I shall grant you three wishes, for you have shown kindness by releasing me."

Ali''s heart swelled with joy, but he paused, thinking carefully about what he truly wanted. He remembered his family and the simple life they led. "Oh mighty genie, for my first wish, I want enough fish to feed my family and share with our neighbors," he said, his voice gentle and sincere.

With a wave of the genie''s hand, the ocean shimmered, and soon, Ali''s boat was filled with fish of every color and size, glistening like jewels in the sunlight. The fisherman felt a warm glow of happiness. "Thank you, dear genie!" he said, smiling brightly. 

For his second wish, he thought of the village children who loved to play by the shore. "I wish for a beautiful playground for the children, filled with laughter and joy!" he declared. The genie nodded, and suddenly, colorful swings, slides, and merry-go-rounds appeared, bringing squeals of delight from the children as they ran towards the new playground.

The village was filled with laughter and happiness, and Ali felt his heart swell with love for his community. But now, he pondered his final wish. What could he ask for that would bring true joy? After a moment, he turned to the genie and said, "For my last wish, I want everyone in our village to always have enough food and be happy together."

The genie smiled, his eyes twinkling like stars. "A beautiful wish, dear fisherman!" With a gentle wave of his hand, he spread a magical glow over the village. From that day on, the fields flourished, and the sea was abundant with fish, ensuring that every family had enough to eat and share.

As the sun began to set, painting the sky with shades of pink and orange, Ali thanked the genie once more. "You have brought us so much joy and abundance!" he said, feeling peaceful inside. The genie nodded and replied, "Remember, dear Ali, true happiness lies in sharing and caring for one another."

With that, the genie slowly returned to his bottle, a soft smile on his face. Ali placed the bottle back into the sea, knowing it would be safe, for the genie was now a part of his heart forever.

As night fell and the stars twinkled above, Ali returned home to his family, feeling grateful and content. He knew that every fish caught and every laugh shared would remind them of their magical adventure. And with that thought, he drifted off to sleep, dreaming of kindness and the peaceful waves of the sea.', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1518709594023-6eab9bab7b23?w=800&h=600&fit=crop', 'en', false, 'en', 'classical', 'adapted from One Thousand and One Nights', NULL, true, 0);
INSERT INTO stories (id, title, summary, moral, full_content, image_url, language, is_translated, original_language, source_type, author_name, author_id, is_public, like_count) VALUES ('14d540cc-3699-46ec-8933-f6e67db0e72b', 'Le petit Chaperon rouge', 'Dans une forêt paisible, une petite fille au chaperon rouge se rend chez sa grand-mère. En chemin, elle rencontre un loup curieux. Ensemble, ils découvrent l''importance de l''amitié et de la gentillesse. Cette belle aventure se termine en douceur, avec des rires et des rêves, sous un ciel étoilé.', 'Moral: "Être gentil et ouvert aux autres peut mener à de belles amitiés. N''oublie jamais de partager des moments joyeux avec ceux qui t''entourent!"', 'Il était une fois, dans un village ensoleillé, une petite fille qui s''appelait le Petit Chaperon Rouge. Elle portait toujours un joli chaperon rouge que sa grand-mère lui avait offert. Un jour, sa maman lui demanda d''apporter un panier de douceurs à sa grand-mère, qui vivait de l''autre côté de la forêt. "Reste sur le chemin et n''oublie pas d''être prudente," lui dit-elle doucement.

Le Petit Chaperon Rouge s''en alla joyeusement, chantant une douce mélodie. La forêt était magnifique, pleine de fleurs colorées et d''oiseaux chantants. Soudain, elle aperçut un loup qui se tenait près d''un arbre. Au lieu d''avoir peur, elle lui sourit et dit : "Bonjour, Monsieur le Loup!"

Le loup, étonné par sa gentillesse, répondit : "Bonjour, petite fille! Que fais-tu dans la forêt?" Le Petit Chaperon Rouge expliqua qu''elle allait rendre visite à sa grand-mère. Le loup, curieux, lui demanda où elle habitait. Il avait une idée en tête, mais il voulait d''abord être gentil.

"Oh, c''est merveilleux!" s''exclama le loup. "Mais prends garde, il y a de jolis chemins dans cette forêt! Pourquoi ne pas prendre celui qui est plein de fleurs?" Le Petit Chaperon Rouge, émerveillée par les belles fleurs, le remercia et s’éloigna joyeusement.

Le loup, quant à lui, décida de prendre un autre chemin pour arriver chez la grand-mère en premier. Mais, au lieu de faire du mal, il frappa doucement à la porte de la maison de la grand-mère. "C''est moi, le Petit Chaperon Rouge," dit-il d''une voix douce. La grand-mère, qui était une femme gentille et sage, lui ouvrit la porte en souriant.

"Bonjour, cher loup! Que veux-tu?" demanda-t-elle. Le loup répondit : "Je viens voir si vous avez besoin d''aide!" La grand-mère, surprise, lui dit qu''elle se sentait bien mais qu''elle adorait avoir de la compagnie. Ils se mirent à discuter et à rire ensemble, partageant des histoires tout en attendant l''arrivée de la petite fille.

Pendant ce temps, le Petit Chaperon Rouge avait cueilli plein de fleurs et se dirigeait vers la maison de sa grand-mère. Lorsqu''elle arriva, elle trouva la porte ouverte. "Bonjour, grand-mère!" appela-t-elle joyeusement. En entrant, elle vit le loup et sa grand-mère assis ensemble, riant et partageant des histoires.

"Oh, quelle surprise!" s''écria le Petit Chaperon Rouge. Le loup se tourna vers elle et dit : "Ne t''inquiète pas, je suis ici pour être ton ami!" La petite fille, ravie de voir sa grand-mère si heureuse, s''assit à côté d''eux. Ensemble, ils partagèrent les douceurs du panier et continuèrent à raconter des histoires drôles jusqu''à ce que le soleil se couche.

Alors que la nuit tombait, le Petit Chaperon Rouge se leva et dit : "Merci, cher loup, pour cette belle journée!" Le loup, souriant, répondit : "Merci à toi d''avoir été si gentille!" La grand-mère ajouta : "Et maintenant, il est temps de dormir, mes chers amis. Les étoiles brillent dans le ciel, et nous ferons de doux rêves ensemble."

Et ainsi, dans la douce lumière de la lune, le Petit Chaperon Rouge, sa grand-mère et le loup s''endormirent paisiblement, entourés de l''amour et de l''amitié, prêts à rêver de nouvelles aventures. 

Et ils vécurent heureux, leur cœur rempli de joie et de rires, sous un ciel rempli d''étoiles scintillantes.', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1516979187457-637abb4f9353?w=800&h=600&fit=crop', 'fr', false, 'fr', 'classical', 'adapted from Charles Perrault', NULL, true, 0);
INSERT INTO stories (id, title, summary, moral, full_content, image_url, language, is_translated, original_language, source_type, author_name, author_id, is_public, like_count) VALUES ('6f02db37-8636-4f67-823c-838db73ca3ee', 'Cendrillon', 'Il était une fois une douce jeune fille nommée Cendrillon, qui vivait avec sa belle-mère et ses demi-sœurs. Malgré les épreuves, elle gardait un cœur pur. Grâce à sa marraine fée, elle assistait à un bal enchanté où elle rencontrait un prince. Avec un peu de magie et beaucoup d''amour, son bonheur se révélait. Une belle histoire de gentillesse et d''espoir pour les rêves d''un doux sommeil.', 'Moral : La gentillesse et l''espoir peuvent réaliser nos rêves, même dans les moments difficiles. Rappelle-toi toujours d''être doux et de croire en toi, car cela peut apporter de belles surprises.', 'Il était une fois, dans un royaume lointain, une jeune fille au cœur pur nommée Cendrillon. Elle vivait avec sa belle-mère et ses deux demi-sœurs, qui, hélas, ne l''aimaient pas. Elles lui donnaient beaucoup de travail et lui faisaient porter de vieux habits. Mais Cendrillon restait toujours douce et gentille, rêvant de jours meilleurs.

Un jour, un grand bal fut annoncé au palais. Le prince invitait toutes les jeunes filles du royaume à venir danser. Cendrillon était très excitée à l''idée d''y aller, mais sa belle-mère lui interdit, la forçant à rester à la maison pour nettoyer.

Dans sa tristesse, Cendrillon pleura doucement dans le jardin. Soudain, sa marraine fée apparut dans un éclat de lumière. "Ne pleure pas, ma chère Cendrillon," dit-elle avec une voix douce. "Je vais t''aider à aller au bal!"

Avec un coup de sa baguette magique, la marraine fée transforma une citrouille en une magnifique carrosse doré et des souris en beaux chevaux. Elle fit aussi une robe étincelante pour Cendrillon, ornée de paillettes qui brillaient comme des étoiles. "Mais souviens-toi, ma chérie, tu dois rentrer avant minuit, car la magie s''évanouira alors," lui rappela-t-elle.

Cendrillon, émerveillée, monta dans le carrosse et se rendit au bal. Lorsqu''elle entra dans la grande salle, tous les yeux se tournèrent vers elle. Le prince, charmé par sa beauté, l''invita à danser. Ensemble, ils tourbillonnaient sous les chandeliers étincelants, riant et s''amusant.

Mais alors que l’horloge commença à sonner minuit, Cendrillon se rappela les paroles de sa marraine. Elle s''échappa du bal, laissant derrière elle une jolie pantoufle de verre. Le prince, désespéré de ne pas savoir qui elle était, décida de tout faire pour la retrouver.

Le lendemain, il parcourut le royaume, demandant à chaque jeune fille d''essayer la pantoufle. Les demi-sœurs de Cendrillon étaient impatientes, mais la pantoufle ne leur allait pas. Enfin, le prince arriva chez Cendrillon. Lorsqu''elle essaya la pantoufle, elle lui allait parfaitement.

Le prince, ébloui par sa beauté et sa bonté, demanda à Cendrillon de l''épouser. Remplie de joie, elle accepta. Ils célébrèrent un grand mariage, entourés de rires et de chants.

Cendrillon et le prince vécurent heureux, et sa marraine fée veillait toujours sur elle. Leurs cœurs étaient remplis d''amour et de bonheur, et chaque nuit, ils s''endormaient sous les étoiles, rêvant de nouvelles aventures à venir.

Et c''est ainsi que Cendrillon trouva son bonheur, prouvant que la gentillesse et l''espoir peuvent transformer les rêves en réalité. Bonne nuit, cher enfant, que tes rêves soient doux et enchanteurs.', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1604004555489-723a93d6ce74?w=800&h=600&fit=crop', 'fr', false, 'fr', 'classical', 'adapted from Charles Perrault', NULL, true, 0);
INSERT INTO stories (id, title, summary, moral, full_content, image_url, language, is_translated, original_language, source_type, author_name, author_id, is_public, like_count) VALUES ('3c35063f-070b-4751-b2db-2b6cab02ec9a', 'La Belle au Bois dormant', 'Il était une fois une belle princesse nommée Aurore, qui, en raison d''une malédiction, s''endormit profondément pendant cent ans. Son doux sommeil fut interrompu par l''amour d''un prince courageux. Ensemble, ils découvrirent la magie de l''amour véritable et la beauté du rêve. Cette histoire douce nous rappelle que l''amour et la gentillesse peuvent surmonter tous les obstacles.', 'Moral : L''amour véritable et la gentillesse peuvent surmonter tous les obstacles. N''oubliez jamais que des rêves doux et de belles amitiés font briller nos cœurs.', 'Il était une fois, dans un royaume lointain, une magnifique princesse nommée Aurore. Elle était si belle que tous les habitants du royaume l’aimaient tendrement. À sa naissance, le roi et la reine organisèrent une grande fête pour célébrer sa venue au monde. Ils invitèrent toutes les fées du royaume, sauf une, qui, fâchée de ne pas avoir été conviée, lança une malédiction sur la princesse : elle se piquerait le doigt sur un fuseau et tomberait dans un profond sommeil lorsque viendrait son seizième anniversaire.

Les fées, heureusement, avaient préparé un contre-sort. La plus gentille des fées annonça que même si Aurore devait s''endormir, son sommeil ne durerait pas pour toujours. Un baiser d''amour véritable la réveillerait.

Les années passèrent, et Aurore grandit entourée d''amour et de douceur. Le jour de son seizième anniversaire, elle se promena dans le palais, pleine de joie, mais elle découvrit une pièce oubliée. À l’intérieur, elle trouva un vieux fuseau. Curieuse, elle toucha le fuseau et, à cet instant, la malédiction se réalisa. Elle s''endormit doucement, comme enveloppée dans un nuage de plumes.

Le royaume entier fut plongé dans un sommeil paisible, et une belle rose commença à pousser autour du château, protégeant le sommeil d''Aurore. Les années passèrent, et beaucoup de princes tentèrent de la réveiller, mais aucun ne réussit. Ils se décourageaient, et le temps semblait s''arrêter.

Un jour, un prince audacieux, attiré par la légende de la belle princesse endormie, décida de se rendre au château. En traversant la forêt, il fut émerveillé par la beauté des roses qui l''entouraient. Lorsqu''il arriva au château, il vit Aurore, endormie et paisible, et sentit son cœur s’emplit d’amour. Il s''approcha d''elle et l''embrassa doucement sur le front.

À cet instant, la magie de l’amour véritable fit son œuvre. Les yeux d''Aurore s''ouvrirent lentement, et elle sourit en voyant le prince. Le royaume tout entier commença à s''éveiller, les oiseaux chantèrent à nouveau et les fleurs s’épanouirent sous le doux soleil.

Aurore et le prince se regardèrent avec tendresse, et le royaume retrouva la joie. Ils célébrèrent leur amour avec une grande fête, où tous dansèrent et rirent sous les étoiles scintillantes.

Et ainsi, Aurore et le prince vécurent heureux, entourés de leurs amis, partageant des histoires et des rêves chaque nuit. Ils savaient que leur amour était aussi fort qu''une douce mélodie, capable de surmonter les plus grands défis.

Alors, chers enfants, lorsque vous fermerez les yeux ce soir, souvenez-vous que l''amour et la gentillesse sont toujours là, prêts à vous envelopper comme un doux rêve. Bonne nuit et faites de beaux rêves.', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1476234251651-f353c1b3e3a1?w=800&h=600&fit=crop', 'fr', false, 'fr', 'classical', 'adapted from Charles Perrault', NULL, true, 0);
INSERT INTO stories (id, title, summary, moral, full_content, image_url, language, is_translated, original_language, source_type, author_name, author_id, is_public, like_count) VALUES ('8b577b4a-1a5b-48ba-a4d3-f0cddd0e472b', 'Le Chat botté', 'Dans un petit village, un humble meunier hérite d''un chat très spécial. Ce chat, astucieux et élégant, aide son maître à réaliser ses rêves. Ensemble, ils apprennent que l''intelligence et l''amitié peuvent surmonter tous les obstacles. Cette douce aventure nous rappelle l''importance de croire en soi et de rester calme, même dans les moments difficiles.', 'Moral : Avec un bon ami à nos côtés, nous pouvons réaliser de grandes choses et surmonter nos peurs. N''oublions jamais de croire en nous-mêmes et en ceux qui nous aiment.', 'Il était une fois, dans un paisible petit village, un meunier qui héritait d''un chat. Ce n''était pas un chat ordinaire, mais un chat botté, élégant et rusé. Le meunier, qui avait toujours travaillé dur au moulin, était un peu inquiet. Que pouvait faire un chat pour lui ? Mais ce chat avait un plan.

Dès le lendemain matin, le chat parla avec son maître : "Ne t''inquiète pas, cher ami. Je vais t''aider à réaliser de grandes choses !" Le meunier, étonné, regarda son chat avec des yeux écarquillés. Il n’avait jamais entendu un chat parler !

Le chat botté sauta sur ses pattes et s’en alla, fier et déterminé. Il trouva un beau sac et se dirigea vers le château du roi. Sur le chemin, il croisa des lapins, des oiseaux et même quelques souris. Mais notre chat n''avait pas peur. Il se mit à penser à la meilleure façon de se faire remarquer.

Arrivé au château, le chat se présenta devant le roi. "Votre Majesté," dit-il, "je suis le chat de ce meunier généreux. Je vous apporte un cadeau : un magnifique lapin tout frais, rien que pour vous !" Le roi, ravi, accepta le cadeau avec un grand sourire. 

Chaque jour, le chat apportait au roi un nouveau cadeau : des oiseaux, des fruits, et même des poissons. Le roi, enchanté par ces présents, commença à se demander qui était ce meunier si spécial. Il voulait le rencontrer.

Pendant ce temps, le chat avait un autre plan. Il dit à son maître : "Ne t’inquiète pas, tout va bien se passer ! Suis-moi au château !" Le meunier était un peu nerveux, mais il faisait confiance à son chat. Ensemble, ils se sont rendus au palais.

Quand ils arrivèrent, le roi reçut le meunier avec chaleur. "Je suis ravi de faire votre connaissance, cher meunier," dit le roi. "Votre chat m''a apporté tant de délices !" Le meunier sourit, réalisant que son chat lui avait ouvert une porte vers le monde merveilleux de la cour.

Le chat botté, voyant que tout se passait bien, décida d''aller un peu plus loin. Il se rendit au bord de la rivière où vivait un grand ogre. "Bonjour, majestueux ogre," commença le chat, avec un ton respectueux. "J''ai entendu dire que vous pourriez vous transformer en n''importe quel animal. Pourriez-vous, par exemple, vous transformer en un petit rat ?" 

L’ogre, fier de ses pouvoirs, accepta de relever le défi. En un clin d''œil, il se transforma en rat. À ce moment-là, le chat bondit et captura le rat agilement, le tenant bien dans ses pattes. "Regardez, Votre Majesté !" cria le chat en retournant au château. Le roi, impressionné, remercia le chat pour sa bravoure.

Le meunier, heureux et reconnaissant, se mit à rêver d''un avenir radieux. Grâce à l''ingéniosité de son chat, il devint le conseiller du roi. Chaque jour, ils avaient des aventures ensemble, mais toujours, ils gardaient le cœur léger et le sourire aux lèvres.

Finalement, la nuit tomba, et le royaume tout entier s''illumina de mille étoiles. Le meunier et son chat se blottirent ensemble, se sentant en sécurité et heureux. Le chat botté, enroulé autour de son maître, murmura : "Tout ira bien, cher ami. Ensemble, nous avons réalisé de grandes choses. Maintenant, il est temps de rêver."

Et ainsi, avec le doux bruit du vent et le scintillement des étoiles, le meunier et son chat s''endormirent paisiblement, prêts à vivre encore de merveilleuses aventures dans leurs rêves.', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1516571748831-5d81767b788d?w=800&h=600&fit=crop', 'fr', false, 'fr', 'classical', 'adapted from Charles Perrault', NULL, true, 0);
INSERT INTO stories (id, title, summary, moral, full_content, image_url, language, is_translated, original_language, source_type, author_name, author_id, is_public, like_count) VALUES ('987603e1-d5c5-4c71-b353-8491c86124c9', 'Le Petit Poucet', 'Dans un petit village, un jeune garçon nommé Poucet, le plus petit d''une fratrie de sept frères, fait preuve de courage et de ruse pour sauver sa famille d''un grand danger. Avec amour et solidarité, ils découvrent que même les plus petits peuvent accomplir de grandes choses. Une histoire douce qui enseigne la force de l''unité et le pouvoir de l''amour fraternel.', 'Moral : Peu importe notre taille, l''important est d''avoir du courage et de travailler ensemble. Avec l''amour et l''amitié, nous pouvons surmonter tous les obstacles.', 'Il était une fois, dans un petit village entouré de forêts enchantées, un jeune garçon nommé Poucet. Poucet était le plus petit des sept frères. Bien qu''il fût minuscule, il avait un grand cœur et une imagination débordante. Ses frères, bien que plus grands et plus forts, avaient souvent tendance à l''ignorer. Mais Poucet savait qu''il était spécial à sa manière.

Un jour, leurs parents, inquiets de la pénurie de nourriture, décidèrent de partir dans la forêt pour chercher du bois. Malheureusement, ils se perdaient et, en entendant des bruits étranges, ils avaient peur. Ils avaient décidé de quitter leurs enfants au village pendant qu''ils se débrouilleraient. Poucet, avec son esprit vif, avait un plan. 

Avant de partir, il s''était glissé hors de la maison en laissant des petits cailloux blancs sur le chemin, pour retrouver son chemin. Les cailloux brillaient de la lumière de la lune et guidaient Poucet et ses frères en toute sécurité. Alors qu''ils marchaient dans la forêt, Poucet leur dit : « Ne vous inquiétez pas, je sais comment rentrer à la maison. »

Soudain, ils rencontrèrent un grand ogre, qui était très méchant. L''ogre voulait capturer les enfants pour les manger. Poucet, avec son intelligence, proposa un plan. Il chuchota à ses frères de rester calmes et de suivre son exemple. 

Quand l''ogre s''approcha, Poucet lui dit avec respect : « Oh grand ogre, nous ne sommes que des enfants, mais nous pouvons vous aider. Si vous nous laissez partir, nous vous apporterons des douceurs de notre village. » L''ogre, intrigué par cette proposition, accepta de les libérer, mais il avait un plan à lui aussi. 

Il invita les enfants chez lui, promettant des friandises. Mais Poucet, avec son courage, avait une idée. Pendant que l''ogre se détournait, il prit la main de ses frères et les guida hors de la maison. Ils coururent aussi vite qu''ils le pouvaient, suivant les cailloux de Poucet. Ils réussirent à retourner à la maison, où leurs parents les attendaient avec des larmes de joie.

Les parents, reconnaissants envers Poucet, réalisèrent que même le plus petit d''entre eux avait sauvé la famille. Ils s''embrassèrent tous, heureux d''être réunis. Poucet, avec un sourire, dit : « Ensemble, nous sommes forts, peu importe notre taille. »

Et alors, dans la douce lumière de la lune, les enfants s''endormirent dans les bras de leurs parents, rêvant d''aventures futures, entourés d''amour et de sécurité. Fin.', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1518709594023-6eab9bab7b23?w=800&h=600&fit=crop', 'fr', false, 'fr', 'classical', 'adapted from Charles Perrault', NULL, true, 0);
INSERT INTO stories (id, title, summary, moral, full_content, image_url, language, is_translated, original_language, source_type, author_name, author_id, is_public, like_count) VALUES ('074dc3c0-0280-4d45-bf33-cebc35158039', 'Riquet à la Houppe', 'Il était une fois un prince nommé Riquet à la Houppe, qui, bien que différent des autres par son apparence, possédait une intelligence et un esprit brillants. Grâce à sa gentillesse et à la magie d''une fée, il découvrit que la beauté se trouve dans le cœur. Une histoire douce sur l''amour, l''acceptation et la valeur de la vraie beauté.', 'Moral : La vraie beauté se trouve dans notre cœur et notre gentillesse. Aimez les autres pour qui ils sont, et vous découvrirez des trésors d''amitié.', 'Il était une fois, dans un royaume lointain, un prince nommé Riquet à la Houppe. Riquet avait une particularité qui le rendait différent des autres enfants : il était un peu laid, avec une grande houppe sur la tête. Mais, contrairement à son apparence, Riquet était doté d''une intelligence exceptionnelle et d''une grande gentillesse. 

Dans ce royaume, tous les enfants jouaient ensemble, riaient et dansaient. Mais Riquet, bien qu''il désirât se joindre à eux, se sentait souvent seul. Un jour, alors qu''il se promenait dans le jardin du château, il rencontra une fée. Cette fée, d''une beauté éclatante, le regarda avec bienveillance. Elle lui dit : « Riquet, ton cœur est pur et ton esprit brille comme les étoiles. Je vais te donner un don spécial. Quand tu rencontreras celle qui t''aimera pour qui tu es, tu lui donneras un pouvoir extraordinaire. » 

Riquet était ravi d''entendre cela. Il remercia la fée et se mit en quête de celle qui pourrait voir au-delà des apparences. Des jours passèrent, et un jour, il apperçut une belle princesse qui pleurait au bord d''un ruisseau. Elle était triste car elle se sentait seule et incomprise. Riquet s''approcha doucement et lui dit : « Ne pleure pas, belle princesse. Parfois, le vrai trésor se trouve à l''intérieur de nous. Je suis ici si tu veux parler. » 

La princesse, surprise par la gentillesse de Riquet, commença à lui raconter ses peines. Ils parlèrent longuement, et Riquet, avec son esprit vif, parvint à la consoler. Peu à peu, la princesse réalisa que Riquet avait un cœur en or. Elle ne voyait plus son apparence, mais l''ami charmant et intelligent qu''il était. 

Leur amitié grandit, et un jour, la fée apparut à nouveau. Elle dit à la princesse : « Grâce à la gentillesse de Riquet, tu peux maintenant voir la beauté intérieure des autres. » La princesse, émerveillée, remercia la fée et, par un doux regard, elle embrassa Riquet. 

En un instant, la houppe de Riquet se transforma en une magnifique couronne dorée, et il devint le prince le plus aimé du royaume. Mais Riquet savait que ce qui importait le plus était le lien spécial qu''il avait créé avec la princesse, qui l''aimait pour qui il était. 

Finalement, le prince et la princesse se marièrent dans une grande célébration, entourés de leurs amis et de leur famille. Ils vécurent heureux, partageant des rires et des histoires chaque soir, enseignant à tous que la beauté réside dans l''amour et l''acceptation. 

Et c''est ainsi que, sous les étoiles scintillantes, Riquet à la Houppe et la princesse trouvèrent leur bonheur, prouvant que le vrai trésor se cache dans le cœur et l''esprit. Bonne nuit, petits rêveurs, que vos rêves soient remplis de beauté et d''amour.', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1516979187457-637abb4f9353?w=800&h=600&fit=crop', 'fr', false, 'fr', 'classical', 'adapted from Charles Perrault', NULL, true, 0);
INSERT INTO stories (id, title, summary, moral, full_content, image_url, language, is_translated, original_language, source_type, author_name, author_id, is_public, like_count) VALUES ('85a27d6b-d2d1-48c0-ae7b-9e8d2b520b94', 'Peau d''Âne', 'Dans un royaume lointain, une belle princesse rêve de liberté. Pour échapper à un destin difficile, elle se cache sous une peau d''âne magique. Avec courage et espoir, elle trouve le chemin vers le bonheur. Suivez son voyage doux et réconfortant vers un avenir radieux, où l''amour et la lumière illuminent son cœur.', 'Moral : Parfois, il faut être courageux pour être soi-même et chercher le bonheur. L''amitié et l''amour peuvent survenir dans les moments les plus inattendus.', 'Il était une fois, dans un royaume lointain, une princesse d''une beauté éclatante. Son père, le roi, était très fier d''elle. Un jour, il lui annonça qu''il souhaitait se remarier. Mais la princesse avait un secret : elle savait que sa belle-mère serait très jalouse de sa beauté. Inquiète de ce qui pourrait arriver, elle prit une grande décision.

La princesse se réfugia dans le jardin du château et demanda à sa fée marraine de l''aider. "Chère fée, je ne peux pas rester ici. Fais quelque chose pour moi!" La fée, avec un sourire doux, lui offrit une peau d''âne magique. "Mets cette peau, ma chère, et tu seras en sécurité. Personne ne te reconnaîtra, et tu pourras partir en paix."

La princesse mit la peau d''âne et, tout à coup, elle se sentit libre. Elle quitta le château en silence, laissant derrière elle les dorures et les inquiétudes du palais. Elle marcha dans les bois, et chaque pas l''emmenait un peu plus loin de son ancien monde.

Un jour, alors qu''elle se reposait près d''un ruisseau, elle entendit la douce mélodie d''un jeune prince qui chantait. Curieuse, elle s''approcha, cachée sous sa peau d''âne. Le prince, avec ses yeux brillants et son cœur pur, remarqua la silhouette étrange mais ne sut pas qui elle était. Il l''invita à s''asseoir à ses côtés.

"Qui es-tu, belle créature?" demanda-t-il doucement. La princesse, bien qu''avec une voix timide, lui répondit : "Je suis juste une pauvre ânesse errante." Le prince, bienveillant, lui parla avec gentillesse, partageant ses rêves et ses histoires de bravoure. Au fur et à mesure qu''ils passaient du temps ensemble, une belle amitié se tissait entre eux.

Les jours passèrent, et la princesse, cachée sous sa peau, trouva du réconfort dans cette nouvelle vie. Elle plantait des fleurs, chantait avec le vent, et se sentait plus joyeuse, même si elle se cachait encore. Mais un jour, le prince remarqua une lueur spéciale dans les yeux de l''ânesse et se mit à se demander qui elle pouvait vraiment être.

Pour découvrir la vérité, il décida de préparer un grand bal au château. Il invita tous les habitants du royaume, y compris l''ânesse mystérieuse. La princesse, excitée mais nerveuse, se demanda si elle devrait y aller. Avec l''encouragement de sa fée marraine, elle accepta de se montrer au bal.

La nuit du bal, la princesse se transforma. En un clin d''œil, elle ôta la peau d''âne, portant une robe étincelante qui brillait comme les étoiles. Quand le prince la vit, il en fut émerveillé. "C''est toi!" s''exclama-t-il, les yeux remplis d''émerveillement. La princesse, radieuse, lui révéla son histoire.

Le prince, touché par son courage, l''embrassa tendrement. Ils dansèrent ensemble toute la nuit, entourés de rires et de joie. Le roi et la reine, émus par leur amour, donnèrent leur bénédiction. Ensemble, ils bâtirent un avenir plein de bonheur, de lumière et de magie.

Et c''est ainsi que la princesse trouva son chemin vers la liberté et l''amour, prouvant que parfois, il faut être courageux pour embrasser son vrai bonheur. En se couchant ce soir-là, elle savait que les rêves d''amour et de douceur l''accompagneraient toujours, la berçant dans un sommeil paisible et serein.', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1604004555489-723a93d6ce74?w=800&h=600&fit=crop', 'fr', false, 'fr', 'classical', 'adapted from Charles Perrault', NULL, true, 0);
INSERT INTO stories (id, title, summary, moral, full_content, image_url, language, is_translated, original_language, source_type, author_name, author_id, is_public, like_count) VALUES ('67722729-0928-4797-aabc-5ffabe7aca2b', 'Les Fées', 'Dans un paisible village, deux sœurs vivent des vies très différentes. L''une est douce et généreuse, tandis que l''autre est fière et égoïste. Un jour, une fée bienveillante récompense la bonté de l''aînée et punit l''arrogance de la cadette. À travers cette histoire, découvrons la magie de la gentillesse et l''importance d''être bon envers les autres.', 'La gentillesse et l''amour sont plus précieux que la beauté extérieure. En prenant soin des autres, nous créons des liens qui rendent notre vie plus belle.', 'Il était une fois, dans un village paisible, deux sœurs qui se ressemblaient comme deux gouttes d''eau, mais qui avaient des cœurs bien différents. L''aînée, nommée Camille, était douce et généreuse. Elle aimait aider les autres et avait toujours le sourire aux lèvres. La cadette, Lucie, était belle et fière, mais elle ne pensait qu''à elle-même. Elle se moquait souvent de sa sœur, ne comprenant pas la valeur de la gentillesse.

Un jour, alors que Camille se promenait dans la forêt, elle rencontra une fée délicate qui scintillait comme les étoiles. La fée, touchée par la bonté de Camille, lui dit : « Ma chérie, pour ta douceur, je vais te donner un don magique. Chaque fois que tu parles, de belles fleurs fleuriront autour de toi. » Camille remercia la fée avec gratitude, émerveillée par ce cadeau.

De retour chez elle, Camille se mit à parler à son chat. À chaque mot, de magnifiques fleurs colorées apparaissaient, remplissant la maison d''un parfum envoûtant. Lucie, jalouse, observa tout cela depuis le coin de la pièce. Elle décida d''en parler à la fée pour obtenir un don encore plus grand.

Elle s''en alla dans la forêt et, trouvant la fée, dit avec arrogance : « Moi aussi, je veux un don ! Je suis plus belle que ma sœur, et je mérite mieux. » La fée, bien que surprise par son attitude, lui répondit calmement : « Très bien, mais souviens-toi que la beauté intérieure compte encore plus. »

Lucie, impatiente, attendit le cadeau. La fée lui offrit un don qui fit apparaître des grenouilles à chaque fois qu''elle parlait. Au début, Lucie trouva cela amusant, mais rapidement, elle s''aperçut que personne ne voulait lui parler. Les gens s''éloignaient d''elle en riant des grenouilles qui bondissaient autour d''elle.

Voyant cela, Camille, avec son cœur tendre, s''approcha de sa sœur. « Ne t''inquiète pas, Lucie, je suis là pour toi. Ensemble, nous pouvons apprendre à être meilleures. » Lucie, touchée par la gentillesse de sa sœur, commença à comprendre que la beauté ne réside pas seulement dans l''apparence, mais dans les actions et les intentions.

Avec le temps, les deux sœurs devinrent inséparables. Lucie apprit à être plus douce et généreuse, et Camille continua de répandre sa bonté. Les fleurs fleuris dans leur maison, et bientôt, les grenouilles disparurent, laissant place à une douce mélodie de rires et d’amour.

